@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home Page";
}

<div class="container-lg">
    <dl>
        <dt class="fs-4 text-black my-2"><i class="bx bx-pencil text-primary fs-4"></i> Project Goal</dt>
        <dd>
            This application replaces the old, outdated Excel macros that were used to convert CSV files. It provides a user-friendly interface for running these conversions and managing the underlying databases.
        </dd>

        <dt class="fs-4 text-black my-2"><i class="bx bx-data text-primary fs-4"></i> FORS IMDS Database</dt>
        <dd>
            This database stores materials and their corresponding IMDS nodes. You can view, create, edit, and delete records.
            <ul>
                <li>Update from A2 + LPCP: opens a form where you upload the LPCP and A2 CSV datasets to initialize or update the database.</li>
                <li>Add new record: lets you add entries manually.</li>
            </ul>
        </dd>
        <dt class="fs-4 text-black my-2"><i class="bx bx-data text-primary fs-4"></i> Porsche Database</dt>
        <dd>
            This database stores materials and their corresponding article names and cross-sections. You can view, create, edit, and delete records.
            <ul>
                <li>Update from CSV: opens a form where you upload the Porsche CSV database (exported from the Porsche Excel file) to initialize or update it.</li>
                <li>Add new record: lets you add entries manually.</li>
            </ul>
        </dd>

        <dt class="fs-4 text-black my-2"><i class="bx bx-wrench text-primary fs-4"></i> FORS Macro</dt>
        <dd>This macro converts FORS BOM CSV files into IMDS BOM CSV files. All output files are bundled into a ZIP archive and downloaded automatically. Any nodes that could not be matched are listed in <i>missing_nodes.csv</i> inside the archive.</dd>
        
        <dt class="fs-4 text-black my-2"><i class="bx bx-wrench text-primary fs-4"></i> Porsche Macro</dt>
        <dd>This macro converts IMDS BOM CSV files into Porsche specific IMDS BOM CSV files. All output files are bundled into a ZIP archive and downloaded automatically. Any article names that could not be matched are listed in <i>missing_articles.csv</i> inside the archive.</dd>
    </dl>
</div>